#!/usr/bin/env sh
# post-commit: deliberate no-op — the version-controlled marker of the
# explicit-gates-only review posture (D2/D4).
#
# Commits in this repo are NOT auto-reviewed. roborev runs only at the explicit
# gates (proposal design review, end-of-implementation `roborev refine`, ad-hoc
# `roborev review`) — never automatically per commit.
#
# How the posture is actually enforced (the earlier "core.hooksPath redirects
# roborev's writes to an inert .git/hooks/" claim was false — roborev FOLLOWS
# core.hooksPath, so its `install-hook`/`init` rewrites THIS file and creates
# .githooks/post-rewrite):
#   1. Auto-review is hook-driven, not daemon-poll: a review is enqueued only
#      when an armed post-commit runs `roborev` post-commit. This no-op stub
#      enqueues nothing, so keeping it the active hook IS the posture.
#   2. scripts/install-hooks.sh restores this stub on every setup/npm install if
#      roborev has armed it (post-commit only — .githooks/post-rewrite's `remap`
#      is left intact for the gates).
#   3. scripts/checks.sh lints .githooks by an explicit kernel-authored allowlist
#      that excludes this file, so a roborev re-arm cannot break the push gate.
# Any change to this stub shows up as a reviewable diff rather than silently
# re-arming auto-review. See WORKFLOW-NOTES.md for the residual re-arm window.
exit 0
